Z||000000||gunnerdd972||11-20-2001||12:36 AM||||In the Fiero gallery, there is a pic of a yellow notchback fiero with a V8 that is longitudinal (I think I spelled that right?).  What kind of transmission is that fiero using.  Does any one have info on this car?  Thanks for the help.||||reg||1
Z||000001||Formula88||11-20-2001||03:19 PM||||Every longitudinal V8 Fiero I've ever seen used the Turbo425 transaxle that was used in the FWD Olds Toronado or Cadillac Eldorado back in the early 70's.  It's basically a FWD version of the Turbo400.||||reg||1
Z||000002||87FieroGTx||11-20-2001||03:54 PM|||| Some ppl have used a Porsche 911 5 speeds in Kitcars but 99% use the Turbo425 in stock fiero frames.<P> With a V8 you "MAY" need to stretch the frame to get the 911 trans to work, I've been thinking about trying to get a supercharged 3800 to work with it longitudinal.<P> Another thing is you have to give up your trunk to get it to work.||||reg||1
